WEBVTT

00:01.618 --> 00:02.642
Oh, come on, Melissa.

00:02.819 --> 00:05.652
How long are you gonna
keep punishing me for this?

00:05.822 --> 00:06.846
Okay, okay.

00:07.023 --> 00:12.120
Once again, uh, I did not technically
have sex with your mother.

00:13.296 --> 00:14.991
You wanna catch me up?

00:15.165 --> 00:17.725
Well, you know Alan
was nailing his receptionist, right?

00:17.901 --> 00:18.925
Yeah.

00:19.102 --> 00:21.366
Apparently, she caught him in bed
with her mother.

00:21.538 --> 00:22.835
What do you know?

00:23.006 --> 00:26.806
I've been calling him that for years,
and now he's up and done it.

00:27.343 --> 00:31.473
I was not responsible for my actions.
I was stoned out of my mind.

00:32.315 --> 00:35.011
You know, that excuse
has never once worked for me.

00:35.785 --> 00:38.481
Me neither, cops or boyfriends.

00:38.955 --> 00:39.979
No. Hey, hey, hey.

00:40.156 --> 00:42.420
Your mother put enough pot
in that banana bread...

00:42.592 --> 00:45.823
...to treat every case of glaucoma
in the San Fernando Valley.

00:45.995 --> 00:48.896
I have a recipe for macaroons,
very similar.

00:51.034 --> 00:53.468
I was so high,
I didn't even know who she was.

00:53.636 --> 00:54.830
We were just colors.

00:56.506 --> 00:58.838
I was red, she was blue.

00:59.008 --> 01:00.566
We were trying to make purple.

01:01.745 --> 01:03.679
My phone's dead.
Could I borrow your cell?

01:03.847 --> 01:06.145
- Sure, it's on the coffee table.
- Thanks.

01:06.316 --> 01:09.114
So bottom line, I was drugged
and molested by your mother...

01:09.285 --> 01:10.513
...and I'm the bad guy.

01:11.888 --> 01:14.755
Man, how many times
have I heard you make this phone call?

01:16.226 --> 01:18.217
Yeah, who'd have thought
of the two of us...

01:18.394 --> 01:21.363
...I'd be the one to end up
in a healthy, stable relationship?

01:23.166 --> 01:26.602
Who is Rachel,
and why is she sending you topless photos?

01:27.370 --> 01:29.770
- Uh...
- Yeah, who'd have thought?

02:02.305 --> 02:06.264
You wanna explain to me why this woman
is sending you naked pictures of herself?

02:06.442 --> 02:08.376
I'd love to explain it.

02:13.983 --> 02:18.113
- Go ahead.
- I said I'd love to, I didn't say I could.

02:18.621 --> 02:21.988
- Are you sleeping with her?
- No. No, of course not.

02:22.158 --> 02:23.318
Then why the pictures?

02:24.294 --> 02:29.857
Uh... Well, my best guess would be that,
like a lot of girls...

02:30.033 --> 02:34.231
...she wanted to show off
her new boob job.

02:34.871 --> 02:36.771
That's your best guess?

02:37.707 --> 02:39.174
Well, you wouldn't understand...

02:39.342 --> 02:43.073
...because clearly,
God has blessed you with this great bounty.

02:43.246 --> 02:45.976
- Damn it, Charlie, I want to know-
- Excuse me, I'm on the phone.

02:46.149 --> 02:51.314
- Shh. Alan's on the phone.
- Don't shush me. Who is this Rachel?

02:51.487 --> 02:52.749
Nobody, really.

02:52.922 --> 02:55.618
I used to go out with her
way, way before you and I met...

02:55.792 --> 02:57.657
...and I fell so deeply in love.

02:57.827 --> 03:00.762
Head over heels in love,
puppy-dog love. Woof.

03:02.532 --> 03:03.556
Hang on, Melissa.

03:03.733 --> 03:06.293
I couldn't hear anything
after "you son of a bitch."

03:06.703 --> 03:09.763
- Does this Rachel know you're engaged?
- Um...

03:09.939 --> 03:13.102
Think long and hard
before you start lying to me.

03:13.643 --> 03:15.804
I was. That's why I said, "Um..."

03:16.346 --> 03:18.371
- Charlie.
- She doesn't know.

03:18.548 --> 03:19.913
Why not?

03:20.083 --> 03:23.644
Boy, you're gonna keep this flapjack
on the griddle, aren't you?

03:28.858 --> 03:33.192
- Berta, would you give us a minute?
- Oh, you're gonna need more than a minute.

03:35.131 --> 03:36.996
So long. I'm gonna miss you.

03:37.901 --> 03:40.768
What are you talking about?
She's not going anywhere, are you?

03:40.937 --> 03:42.495
Where are you going? Chelsea.

03:43.673 --> 03:45.937
- Chelsea, wait.
- Can't we just put this behind us?

03:46.109 --> 03:49.010
I swear, I'll never make out
with your mother again.

03:50.280 --> 03:53.545
Let's face it, Charlie. We both knew
you were gonna blow it eventually.

03:53.716 --> 03:56.810
I didn't.
I had my suspicions, but I wasn't sure.

03:56.986 --> 03:59.352
I wish I could say the same. Goodbye.

04:00.657 --> 04:03.182
- Oh, please don't leave.
- Oh, please don't hang up.

04:03.359 --> 04:05.088
ALAN &amp; CHARLIE:
I love you.

04:06.863 --> 04:08.888
And I love you too.

04:14.570 --> 04:15.867
Sure you don't want a drink?

04:16.039 --> 04:20.237
No. When I'm depressed,
alcohol just makes me feel worse.

04:20.410 --> 04:23.902
Yeah, see, the trick is to drink past that.

04:25.181 --> 04:28.207
It's not a sprint, it's a marathon.

04:29.385 --> 04:32.582
You ever think we're both doomed
to grow old alone and unloved?

04:32.755 --> 04:35.952
A couple of pathetic bachelors
with no one to talk to but each other?

04:37.493 --> 04:39.984
You ought to do ads for this stuff.

04:41.531 --> 04:44.193
So you gonna tell me what happened
with Chelsea?

04:45.168 --> 04:47.102
I can show you.

04:47.904 --> 04:51.431
Chelsea found this on my phone.

04:51.607 --> 04:54.804
I ask you,
is that worth breaking an engagement?

05:01.384 --> 05:03.375
It's worth breaking a spine.

05:04.554 --> 05:08.957
- Were you sleeping with this girl?
- No, no. She just sent me a few pictures.

05:09.125 --> 05:11.093
Oh, well, then why did you keep them?

05:13.229 --> 05:15.254
All right, all right, all right.

05:15.431 --> 05:19.367
But you gotta understand
the message that this sends to Chelsea.

05:19.535 --> 05:21.935
Other than, you know:

05:22.105 --> 05:23.572
"Got milk."

05:28.044 --> 05:30.706
- But I'm not cheating.
- There are other forms of cheating.

05:30.880 --> 05:34.247
There's flirting,
there's fantasizing about other women.

05:34.417 --> 05:37.477
- Oh, come on. Fantasizing is not cheating.
- To women it is.

05:37.653 --> 05:41.953
They don't like the idea that you're
mentally replacing them with someone else.

05:42.592 --> 05:45.254
What if I'm mentally supplementing them
with someone else?

05:46.362 --> 05:49.126
You know, like I'm making love to Chelsea,
and in my mind...

05:49.298 --> 05:51.562
...Rachel here is just helping out.

05:55.805 --> 05:58.774
She does look very helpful.

05:59.642 --> 06:02.873
Nevertheless, I can understand
why Chelsea would take a dimmer view.

06:03.046 --> 06:04.843
Yeah, well, I think she overreacted.

06:05.014 --> 06:07.278
In fact, I think she owes me an apology.

06:07.450 --> 06:10.476
You're just gonna sit here
and wait till she comes crawling back?

06:10.653 --> 06:12.644
Yes, I am.

06:12.822 --> 06:16.485
And then, because hell
will long since have frozen over...

06:16.659 --> 06:18.456
...we can go ice-skating.

06:19.095 --> 06:21.427
It's good that you have a plan.

06:22.432 --> 06:24.195
Now, if you will pardon me...

06:24.367 --> 06:26.665
...I have to go pick up Jake
at his mother's.

06:26.836 --> 06:29.964
Oh, good. Just what we need
to brighten up our weekend.

06:30.139 --> 06:34.303
A large, sullen teenager
with gas and questionable hygiene.

06:34.811 --> 06:37.336
There's nothing questionable about it.

06:44.754 --> 06:46.779
There we go.

06:46.956 --> 06:48.947
Over the hump.

06:52.328 --> 06:55.354
JUDITH: She's my mother, Herb.
I want her here when I have the baby.

06:55.765 --> 06:58.825
Well, I don't need yet another woman
in this house yelling at me...

06:59.001 --> 07:00.161
...calling me an idiot.

07:00.336 --> 07:02.099
JUDITH:
My mother doesn't yell, you idiot.

07:02.271 --> 07:04.466
I'm gonna let that pass
because you're pregnant.

07:04.640 --> 07:06.767
JUDITH:
Don't you dare blame this on hormones.

07:08.144 --> 07:10.942
What's my alternative, Judith?
Accept the fact that I'm an idiot?

07:13.816 --> 07:16.444
- Oh, hey, Alan.
- Is this a bad time?

07:17.053 --> 07:18.884
They're all bad.

07:19.956 --> 07:22.254
Seven and a half months of bad.

07:22.425 --> 07:25.690
JUDITH: Don't you walk away from me.
- Oh, I'm sorry, I was answering the door.

07:25.862 --> 07:28.854
That's what we idiots do
when we hear a doorbell.

07:29.365 --> 07:31.890
Hi, Dad. Bye, Mom. Good luck, Herb.

07:32.468 --> 07:35.460
Bye, Jake. Wish I was going with you.

07:41.978 --> 07:44.708
I knew it
as soon as it came out of my mouth.

07:52.989 --> 07:55.116
I could get used to this.

07:55.791 --> 07:57.281
Don't.

07:59.829 --> 08:03.959
&lt;i>As far as Charlie's concerned,
mi casa es mi casa.&lt;/i>

08:05.101 --> 08:07.569
All right, I've ordered your pizza.
I'm going home.

08:07.737 --> 08:09.329
Thanks, Berta.

08:10.306 --> 08:12.331
Ordering a pizza and going home.

08:12.508 --> 08:14.942
Two of the three things you want
in a woman.

08:15.645 --> 08:18.136
And you wonder
why Chelsea dumped you.

08:18.681 --> 08:20.376
I'll tell you what I wonder.

08:20.550 --> 08:22.950
I wonder how you could
possibly get stoned enough...

08:23.119 --> 08:26.111
...to stick your tongue
in the mouth of a 60-year-old woman.

08:31.994 --> 08:33.256
Zing.

08:35.865 --> 08:39.824
Boy, I just love this male bonding,
giving each other the old business.

08:40.469 --> 08:41.493
The old business?

08:41.671 --> 08:46.438
&lt;i>Yeah, you know,
the needle, the zets, the razzmatazz.&lt;/i>

08:47.076 --> 08:48.907
Herb, I gotta ask you something.

08:49.078 --> 08:52.138
Are there any other guys
you hang out with?

08:52.315 --> 08:54.806
Oh, sure. I have my peeps.

08:54.984 --> 08:59.887
There's my water-polo league,
the guys down at the model-train shop.

09:00.056 --> 09:04.288
Oh, and my barbershop quartet.
Although I can't have them over anymore.

09:04.460 --> 09:05.722
Why not?

09:05.895 --> 09:08.864
Four-part harmony
triggers Judith's migraines.

09:09.265 --> 09:11.563
Plus, mustaches creep her out.

09:11.734 --> 09:14.100
Not just mustaches,
any facial hair whatsoever.

09:14.270 --> 09:16.397
- Right, except eyebrows.
- Neatly trimmed.

09:16.572 --> 09:18.836
Right, the two-finger rule.

09:20.743 --> 09:25.703
Huh. Chelsea had a two-finger rule.
Nothing to do with eyebrows though.

09:26.449 --> 09:28.076
All right, I'll see you later.

09:28.251 --> 09:30.378
- Where you going?
- To the pier with Celeste.

09:30.553 --> 09:33.021
- Who's Celeste?
- My girlfriend. She lives next door.

09:33.189 --> 09:36.420
- She pretty?
- She's gorgeous and smart and popular.

09:36.592 --> 09:39.060
- No kidding.
- We don't get it either.

09:41.931 --> 09:45.731
- Maybe she's punishing her father.
- Let's hope so.

09:48.271 --> 09:51.832
I'm just the stepdad here, but shouldn't you
tell him what time to be home?

09:52.008 --> 09:54.704
I don't have to. I know her father.

09:55.745 --> 09:57.542
Hey, Jake.

09:59.815 --> 10:01.112
Hello, sir.

10:02.918 --> 10:04.852
Celeste, Jake's here.

10:05.321 --> 10:06.345
So how have you been?

10:06.522 --> 10:10.720
We're walking to the pier, we're gonna
play Skee-Ball, and we'll be back by 11.

10:11.727 --> 10:13.957
You're damn right you will.

10:22.171 --> 10:26.107
- Come on, it's freezing out here.
- Shouldn't we put out the cigars?

10:27.276 --> 10:28.743
Why?

10:28.911 --> 10:31.675
Uh, because we're not allowed to smoke
in the house?

10:33.916 --> 10:34.940
It's my house.

10:35.117 --> 10:38.109
We can smoke cigars,
we can smoke salmon, whatever we want.

10:39.822 --> 10:41.050
Are you sure?

10:41.223 --> 10:43.919
Relax, no whiny broad
is gonna nag at you.

10:44.093 --> 10:47.392
Herb, make sure you use an ashtray
and a coaster.

10:50.199 --> 10:51.393
I stand corrected.

10:53.202 --> 10:54.533
Zing.

10:55.571 --> 10:56.731
Gotcha.

10:59.909 --> 11:02.469
Oh, this is gonna be a long night.

11:05.448 --> 11:07.177
- Hi, Charlie.
- Oh, God.

11:07.350 --> 11:10.945
- What did the little knucklehead do?
- Nothing. Jake said you were hanging out.

11:11.120 --> 11:13.247
- I thought you might want company.
- Come on in.

11:13.422 --> 11:15.219
I baked snickerdoodles, if you're hungry.

11:17.393 --> 11:20.829
- You baked snickerdoodles?
- Yeah. Why's that funny?

11:23.566 --> 11:25.124
It's not.

11:26.335 --> 11:28.132
You know Alan, and this is Herb.

11:28.304 --> 11:29.498
- Hi.
- Hi.

11:29.672 --> 11:31.970
Make yourself comfortable.
Something to drink?

11:32.141 --> 11:34.575
I wouldn't say no to an appletini.

11:35.411 --> 11:38.505
An appletini? Ha, ha.
My brother drinks appletinis.

11:39.448 --> 11:41.439
Why is that funny?

11:41.917 --> 11:43.441
It's not.

11:44.320 --> 11:46.618
One appletini, coming up.

11:47.189 --> 11:49.749
He can get away with it. You can't.

11:51.293 --> 11:53.090
So how do you know Charlie and Alan?

11:53.262 --> 11:57.528
- Oh, I'm married to Alan's ex-wife.
- No kidding. And you hang out?

11:57.700 --> 11:59.031
- Yeah.
- Sure.

12:00.035 --> 12:03.869
Wow. I couldn't be friends with the man
who's putting it to my ex.

12:08.611 --> 12:11.842
Well, to be fair,
there hasn't been a lot of putting lately.

12:14.850 --> 12:17.944
And after the baby's born,
there will be even less.

12:18.320 --> 12:20.151
How's that possible?

12:20.322 --> 12:22.790
Not only will she not let you touch her...

12:22.958 --> 12:25.518
...she'll interrupt you
while you're touching yourself.

12:33.035 --> 12:34.502
Oh?

12:35.137 --> 12:37.230
I had to start showering at the Y.

12:39.842 --> 12:42.902
- Okay, one appletini.
- Thank you.

12:43.646 --> 12:47.173
- What are you guys talking about?
- Masturbating at the YMCA.

12:52.455 --> 12:55.151
Really? Just talk, right?

12:55.324 --> 12:57.656
Yeah, but the night is young.

12:58.694 --> 13:00.457
So, Jerome...

13:00.629 --> 13:04.030
...solve one of the great mysteries
of life for us.

13:05.501 --> 13:07.492
What does your daughter see in Jake?

13:08.003 --> 13:11.404
You know,
I've been asking myself the same thing.

13:11.574 --> 13:13.337
Maybe she's punishing me.

13:15.544 --> 13:18.638
- No offense.
- None taken.

13:19.048 --> 13:21.016
We're way ahead of you.

13:21.851 --> 13:24.445
You know, my wife and I are having a girl.
Any advice?

13:24.987 --> 13:29.048
Yeah. Before your daughter starts dating,
um, bulk up.

13:31.794 --> 13:33.421
Okay.

13:35.231 --> 13:37.961
Boy, remember
when we first started dating?

13:38.133 --> 13:40.863
Yup. Eighth grade, Louise Miller.

13:41.036 --> 13:42.970
Oh, ninth grade, Maxine Chernakoff.

13:43.138 --> 13:45.436
Sixth grade, Mrs. Terapotta.

13:51.480 --> 13:54.005
It wasn't actually a date.

13:54.183 --> 13:56.651
Nowadays, she'd probably go to jail.

13:57.152 --> 13:58.642
So, what about you, Herb?

13:59.021 --> 14:02.047
- What about me, what?
- Your first date. Junior high? High school?

14:02.224 --> 14:06.058
Oh, college, freshman year.
I was kind of a geek in high school.

14:06.228 --> 14:07.820
Hard to believe.

14:08.430 --> 14:10.455
No, really. They called me Big Bird.

14:13.602 --> 14:15.160
So, what happened in college?

14:15.571 --> 14:18.904
I stopped wearing yellow shirts
and lowered my standards.

14:19.742 --> 14:22.267
Okay, okay, here's one.

14:22.444 --> 14:26.005
First sexual experience
that was not traditional intercourse.

14:26.549 --> 14:29.677
- What are we talking about here?
- You know what I'm talking about.

14:29.852 --> 14:31.285
Boy Scouts.

14:43.299 --> 14:44.732
What?

14:44.900 --> 14:47.460
Oh. Zing.

14:50.139 --> 14:54.166
Alan, when did you
first take your oral exams?

14:54.743 --> 14:57.041
I don't think I should say.

14:57.212 --> 14:58.440
- Why not?
- I just don't.

14:58.614 --> 15:02.015
- Come on, we're all friends. Who was it?
- Your wife.

15:03.752 --> 15:05.947
So your first time doing that
was with Judith?

15:08.023 --> 15:09.786
Hey, me too.

15:12.561 --> 15:13.687
Me too.

15:18.334 --> 15:19.858
Just kidding. Zing. Zing.

15:23.839 --> 15:27.331
What is "zing"?
Is that some type of white-guy slang?

15:27.610 --> 15:28.634
Quite possibly.

15:28.811 --> 15:32.747
My barbershop quartet does a killer version
of "Zing! Went the Strings of My Heart."

15:32.915 --> 15:35.145
Real showstopper.

15:35.818 --> 15:37.513
Kind of like that story.

15:38.687 --> 15:40.018
Zing.

15:41.657 --> 15:42.817
Did I get that one right?

15:46.261 --> 15:47.489
Oh, good. Finally.

15:47.663 --> 15:49.324
- Hookers?
- Pizza.

15:49.498 --> 15:52.160
Oh. That's nice too.

15:53.602 --> 15:56.571
- Hey, Mr. Harper.
- Oh, hey, Gordon. It's been a long time.

15:56.739 --> 15:59.264
- Yeah, two years.
- So, what you been up to?

15:59.441 --> 16:01.033
Well, I finished night school...

16:01.210 --> 16:04.077
...got my business degree,
met an amazing girl, got married...

16:04.246 --> 16:08.410
...landed a great job as a stockbroker, the
company went under, my wife left me, uh...

16:08.584 --> 16:10.518
...and that will be 28.50.

16:13.989 --> 16:16.423
Oh, man, I'm sorry.

16:16.592 --> 16:18.617
- You want a drink?
- Why stop now?

16:20.796 --> 16:22.388
Come on in.

16:26.201 --> 16:28.101
Hey, everybody, this is Gordon.

16:28.270 --> 16:30.295
- His wife left him.
- Hey, Gordon.

16:30.472 --> 16:33.373
- Welcome to the Losers' Lounge.
- Heh, heh. Glad to be here.

16:33.542 --> 16:36.875
The topic of discussion
is first nontraditional sexual experience.

16:37.046 --> 16:38.638
Bible camp.

16:40.749 --> 16:44.446
- Where you guys want me to put these?
- Oh, here, let me move the snickerdoodles.

16:44.887 --> 16:46.582
Oh, snickerdoodles.

16:47.289 --> 16:48.916
- You don't like them?
- No, no, I do.

16:49.091 --> 16:53.255
It's just that my wife used to call me
her little snickerdoodle. Heh, heh.

16:53.429 --> 16:56.227
- You're kidding.
- Well, no, not all of me.

16:56.398 --> 16:58.161
It was her little nickname for my, uh...

17:01.403 --> 17:04.634
Oh, that is a terrible name for a penis.

17:05.708 --> 17:09.269
- Oh, yeah? What did your wife call yours?
- Mr. Roundtree.

17:16.885 --> 17:18.409
Richard Roundtree?

17:19.688 --> 17:21.349
The guy who played Shaft?

17:21.523 --> 17:23.616
- Oh, right.
- Oh, yes.

17:23.792 --> 17:26.283
That's way better than "snickerdoodle."

17:27.463 --> 17:30.227
Judith calls mine "that thing."

17:30.833 --> 17:33.495
As in "Get that thing away from me"?

17:34.436 --> 17:37.269
- Yeah, how did you know?
- Just a guess.

17:40.275 --> 17:42.140
Okay, I'm out of here.

17:42.644 --> 17:43.906
Where you going?

17:44.079 --> 17:47.810
Someplace where I'm not knee-deep
in pathetic, penis-naming, sad sacks.

17:50.319 --> 17:51.581
No offense.

17:51.754 --> 17:53.915
- None taken.
- None taken.

17:54.623 --> 17:56.181
Let's go, King Snake.

18:10.706 --> 18:13.038
- What do you want?
- Just listen.

18:14.376 --> 18:16.844
Rachel? Hey, it's Charlie.

18:17.012 --> 18:19.640
Look, about the pictures you sent me-

18:19.815 --> 18:21.806
No, no. No, they were very nice.

18:23.685 --> 18:25.744
Yeah, real artsy.

18:27.089 --> 18:29.649
But the thing is,
I'm kind of engaged now.

18:31.660 --> 18:36.324
I am definitely engaged now,
so you shouldn't send me any more.

18:37.633 --> 18:39.999
Doesn't matter who asked for them.

18:41.904 --> 18:44.668
The point is, I am no longer interested
in anyone's boobs...

18:44.840 --> 18:46.273
...other than my fiancée's.

18:47.709 --> 18:50.405
No, I'm not gonna send you
a picture of hers.

18:52.147 --> 18:53.842
Right?

18:54.817 --> 18:55.943
No.

18:57.152 --> 19:00.053
- Okay, take care.
- Thank you, Charlie.

19:00.856 --> 19:03.620
I just want you to know
how much you mean to me.

19:03.792 --> 19:05.453
Did you delete the pictures?

19:06.295 --> 19:10.425
Um, I guess there's a case
to be made for that.

19:14.369 --> 19:17.497
- What are you doing? Press delete.
- Hang on.

19:17.673 --> 19:19.231
I'm imprinting them in my memory.

19:21.176 --> 19:24.475
Delete, delete, delete. Look, I'm deleting.

19:26.949 --> 19:28.883
&lt;i>GORDON &amp; HERB Zing!
Dear, when you smiled at me&lt;/i>

19:29.051 --> 19:30.712
&lt;i>- Zing!
- I heard a melody&lt;/i>

19:30.886 --> 19:32.877
&lt;i>- Zing!
- It haunted me from the start&lt;/i>

19:33.255 --> 19:34.654
&lt;i>- The start
- The start&lt;/i>

19:34.823 --> 19:36.518
&lt;i>Zing!
- Something inside of me&lt;/i>

19:36.692 --> 19:38.387
&lt;i>Zing!
- Started a symphony&lt;/i>

19:38.560 --> 19:40.323
&lt;i>Zing! Went the strings of my heart&lt;/i>

19:41.997 --> 19:43.760
&lt;i>Zing!
'Twas like a breath of spring&lt;/i>

19:43.932 --> 19:45.331
&lt;i>Zing!
I heard a robin sing&lt;/i>

19:45.767 --> 19:47.166
&lt;i>Zing!
About a nest set apart&lt;/i>

19:47.336 --> 19:49.361
No wonder they're all alone.

19:49.538 --> 19:51.199
&lt;i>Zing!
All nature seemed to be&lt;/i>

19:51.373 --> 19:53.102
&lt;i>Zing!
- In perfect harmony&lt;/i>

19:53.275 --> 19:56.870
&lt;i>Zing! Went the strings of my heart&lt;/i>

20:07.522 --> 20:10.286
&lt;i>Who is the man that would risk his neck&lt;/i>

20:10.459 --> 20:11.892
&lt;i>For his brother man?&lt;/i>

20:12.060 --> 20:13.084
&lt;i>Shaft&lt;/i>

20:13.262 --> 20:14.593
&lt;i>Right on&lt;/i>

20:14.763 --> 20:17.561
&lt;i>- I heard this cat Shaft is one bad mother-
- Shut your mouth&lt;/i>

20:17.733 --> 20:19.860
&lt;i>- I'm talking about Shaft
- Then we can dig it&lt;/i>

20:20.269 --> 20:22.100
&lt;i>He's a complicated man&lt;/i>

20:22.437 --> 20:24.803
No, I can't do this.

20:25.340 --> 20:27.808
She has to take me back.
